 or an  unsecured loan what is the actual offer  to the investor or is it going to be a  joint venture now a joint venture is  just a case of they're putting the money  in and then you're going to split the  profits maybe you can split the profits  50 50. in which case how is it going to  be structured you could set it up in a  company where you could say look we're  going to set up a company together  you're going to have 50 ownership to the  company i'm going to have 50 ownership  you're going to put 100 grand in  i'm then going to use that 100 grand to  buy a property to fix it up to sell it  and then the whatever the profit we we  make the company will then divvy that up  50 50. if you're gonna do that what  security has the investor got usually  when they put the money into the company  that would be a director's loan or you  might have a shares and b shares with  the company so you just need to make  sure that when you're pitching this it's  not just about the deal the deal being  good it's also about the deal being well  structured so that it's safe and secure  for the investor so that's the very  first thing to think about before  raising capital and before trying to  raise finance from investors next thing  once you've got that set up you've got  your deal you've thought about the  structure you've got a good structure  set up which is fair and secure for the  investor next thing you need to do is  before going crazy on social media and  running your mouth everywhere and trying  to pitch everybody for deals i would  suggest  contact some of your friends and family  that you know or you suspect have got  money this is genius now because rather  than actually asking them for money  should never do that  because it's awkward if they're your  friend or your mom  and you go hey mom um  i've got this deal um could you give me  a hundred grand it's awkward because if  she says no  she might fear that it would damage your  relationship if she says yes  she might be it's just a bit awkward  asking for money so here's what you do  instead you contact your friends and  your family and your loved ones that you  know what you think or you suspect might  have money and you ask them for their  advice so you say hey  auntie hey uncle hey friends hey bob  next door  cat i've got this deal that i'm working  on at the moment and i'm i'm just  structuring everything and i'd really  love to get your opinion would it be  possible that i could meet you for a  coffee and i can share the deal with you  and then maybe you can just let me know  if you've got any advice or any pointers  because i really value your advice  who's gonna say no to that right  your mom or whoever will be like yeah  sure thing now this is not being  manipulative by the way this is just  making it easy for them  to walk away from the deal because if  you say to them hey i've got this deal  do you want to invest it's awkward but  if you say hey i've got this deal i'd  love to talk to you about it get your  advice then what you do is you show them  the deal you show them how freaking  amazing it is and go look it's gonna  make this much money you show them and  hopefully they'll be impressed and then  you say also  here's how we're gonna be structuring it  i'm actually looking for a joint venture  partner i'm looking for someone to put a  hundred grand in this is how we're going  to be structuring it do you think that  seems fair okay cool and then you can  say well look if you know anybody that  you think might be able to be a suitable  joint venture partner or an investor um  you know do let me know because i am  looking for an investor  that's it  nothing else  if they don't bite if they don't go well  you know what  we could be interested then they're not  interested so you never had to ask in  the first place just leave it move on  once you've exhausted your friends and  family and you've spoken to them if no  one's interested hopefully they will be  that's when you can start their  networking going on social media talking  about the deal be careful of not posting  specifics when you're posting on social  media it's against the fca regulations  for you to post a deal and say i'm  guaranteeing to offer x percent you  can't do that but what you can do is you  can post the deal and just say hey i've  got this deal i'm looking for partners  if anyone's interested dm me we could  have a chat you can go to networking  events and you can normally when you go  to a lot of networking events if it's a  specific business networking event  opportunity you usually have like 60  seconds to stand up and just pitch your  business so you can stand up and say hey  i've just secured a property which we're  going to be splitting into four flats  it's got 100 000 pounds profit i'm  currently looking for a partner with  somebody that's got some capital if you  know anybody come and see me in the  break  easy right this is how you do it another  thing i want to say on social media as  well the final point is build your brand  on social media every time you do a deal  every time you even view a house every  time you do anything  that shows that you're in the game  you're in the business you're getting  results post it on social media share  your journey and then all of your  contacts will be like oh this person is  doing deals this person's doing well  never grumble  don't [ __ ] online about oh i hate the  prime minister and [ __ ] and go on about  how hard life is and how depressed you  are because if you do that what's going  to happen is you're going to be  repulsing your potential future  investors so this is not about betraying  a fake life or fake it till you make it  this is about build your brand and show  people what you're doing to build up  your reputation  get good deals structure it right and  that hopefully was a useful video  [Music]  you
 

